(A function may read a top-level thing declared below the call. Before
 the declaration runs, its text, list, map and buffer fields already hold
 their defaults; the declaration then gives the thing its defaults again.)

A thing called note has
  a text called title is "shopping",
  a list called items is ["eggs"],
  a map called counts,
  a buffer called body is "milk".

To 'look at the note'.
  Print errand.
  append "bread" to errand's items.
  Print errand's items.

'look at the note'.
a note called errand.
Print errand.
